{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/983778-something-gross-in-legacies-the-sublime","id":983778,"title":"Something gross in Legacies: The Sublime","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-07T23:19:23-07:00","id":983778,"title":"Something gross in Legacies: The Sublime","content":"Look, I kind of hate to do this, and it's not really like the other complaints. We've talked about the difference between preferences, design criticisms, and genuinely harmful things...and there's something in Sublime that I have to kind of say was the last one. It's a book that had a lot of legacies I liked, and unfortunately it showed up in the writeup for one of the ones I liked. The final page of the Threnodists writeup shows the sample character using his powers to, based on the picture, ogle a woman in the shower, and it...really kind of left a bad taste in my mouth. I know it's a minor thing, but it just really leaves a sour note for the whole book. I mean, you have a limited number of art pieces you can put in...and you waste one of them on drawing a leering man humiliate a woman in the shower. He isn't even presented as a villain or anything, his writeup is basically &quot;look at this Zany Cool Uncle!&quot;. Again, I know it's probably a minor thing, but it just...always bothered me.<br /> <br /> This might be a weird question, but I have it as a PDF, and is there any way I could just...edit it to remove that page? Because, as I said, the rest of the book has a lot I like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T23:32:05-07:00","id":983784,"title":"","content":"Honestly, the biggest question that comes to mind for me is why the guy is scrying someone who has the ability to see him through a scrying window. I mean in 1e you can't even perceive scrying windows without a mystical means of doing so, so is he scrying a cabal mate of his and just happened to check in at the wrong time or what? As for editing the book in PDF form, good question, let me check the internet.<br /> <br /> Edit: Simplest/Quickest answer I'm seeing is yes, but you need software designed to do it. There's probably reliable, free programs floating around somewhere if you look for it specifically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 10-08-2016, 02:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T05:01:12-07:00","id":983855,"title":"","content":"Yeah. It isn't the best, and we wouldn't put an image like that in an Onyx Path book (Sublime was one of the first - I think maybe third? - books for Awakening a decade ago.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T17:14:21-07:00","id":985138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/983778-something-gross-in-legacies-the-sublime?p=983855#post983855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. It isn't the best, and we wouldn't put an image like that in an Onyx Path book (Sublime was one of the first - I think maybe third? - books for Awakening a decade ago.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And honestly, I kinda hope Onyx Path never really does Legacy books again.<br /> <br /> They are <i>boooooring</i>, as opposed to more interesting books that might just also contain a few Legacies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T17:53:31-07:00","id":985164,"title":"","content":"I liked the legacy books, just saying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T19:24:28-07:00","id":985214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/983778-something-gross-in-legacies-the-sublime?p=985138#post985138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> And honestly, I kinda hope Onyx Path never really does Legacy books again.<br /> <br /> They are <i>boooooring</i>, as opposed to more interesting books that might just also contain a few Legacies.</div> </div> </div> </div>In 1st edition they were boring and you would maybe find 3 legacies to use but to be fair they werent as bad as the Bloodlines books.<br /> <br /> However now in 2nd, i kinda wish they release one with all the convertions to 2e so as to not have to wait for scraps between books ala werewolf. Core with a token mention of them, and the first sourcebook is mostly fluffy bits, LOTs of mention of them with no mechanics and then is up to waste more wordcount on locations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 10-10-2016, 10:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T23:25:54-07:00","id":985291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/983778-something-gross-in-legacies-the-sublime?p=985214#post985214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In 1st edition they were boring and you would maybe find 3 legacies to use but to be fair they werent as bad as the Bloodlines books.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the Lodge books were the absolute, worst offenders.<br /> <br /> Right now, I primarily want fluffy books with delicious new Merits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T23:44:59-07:00","id":985297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/983778-something-gross-in-legacies-the-sublime?p=985214#post985214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In 1st edition they were boring and you would maybe find 3 legacies to use but to be fair they werent as bad as the Bloodlines books.</div> </div> </div> </div>I loved the Bloodline books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T01:41:31-07:00","id":985320,"title":"","content":"I really liked the legacies books as well, but would prefer if every book came with 2-3 legacies relevant to the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7463-toine","name":"Toine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7463_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T03:38:56-07:00","id":985342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/983778-something-gross-in-legacies-the-sublime?p=985297#post985297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I loved the Bloodline books.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ymmv, personally reading them was a long checklist of &quot;unusable, unusable, a bullet in the foot, a bullet in the foot, unusable, who the hell play this?, who the hell play this?, OH something useful!, unusable, unusable, so on and so on&quot; Many were incredible laser focus concepts, like vampire in a hospital.....which we got like one for each clan because thats....incredible popular and party friendly concept? Or just plain bad mechanics like the no-tzimices, the norvegi. Get the incredible crippling flaw of no fangs in exchange for a worse version of gangrel claws.....yeah no.<br /> <br /> I kind of prefer the model of say, shadowrun for the new edition. In the sense they release the convertions from the previous ones as &quot;quickly&quot; (because catalyst labs) and the go on to make new stuff. I would buy the hell of a book that was just &quot;Gifts, lodge and rites: From 1st to 2nd&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 10-11-2016, 06:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T07:34:03-07:00","id":985408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/983778-something-gross-in-legacies-the-sublime?p=985297#post985297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I loved the Bloodline books.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I find the Bloodline books infinitely better and more useful than the Legacy books.<br /> <br /> And then I see the Legacy books as <i>waaaaaaay</i> better than the Lodge books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T08:26:37-07:00","id":985433,"title":"","content":"I liked the Legacy and Bloodline books because they appeal to both my inner with crunch-happy mechanics whore and my inner fluff-happy setting whore by presenting a series of varied, mechanically-supported organizations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T09:17:44-07:00","id":985460,"title":"","content":"I loved the legacy books. The concepts were frequently pretty great, the mechanical execution less so (Clavicularius? ug).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/358-emanantvolition","name":"EmanantVolition","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T11:59:15-07:00","id":985573,"title":"","content":"Something to consider as we drift away from the initial complaint, is that the newer production models allows Onyx Path to take a middle ground approach to these sorts of things:<br /> <br /> They can sell Legacies individually/in small groups as cheap pdfs, and sell a big book of them. The big book will be cheaper than each individually, but if you only find 1/3 of them worth using, you can just get those.<br /> <br /> While I like mechanics (including Legacies) presented in supplements to highlight their themes, I also appreciate having the big books of z-splats because there's a lot of cool ideas that might not get published because they're not appropriate to a specific supplement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T16:05:24-07:00","id":985745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/983778-something-gross-in-legacies-the-sublime?p=985138#post985138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> And honestly, I kinda hope Onyx Path never really does Legacy books again.<br /> <br /> They are <i>boooooring</i>, as opposed to more interesting books that might just also contain a few Legacies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of us adored the Legacy books and learned a lot about making our own by following the themes over a course of a book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T16:08:48-07:00","id":985749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/983778-something-gross-in-legacies-the-sublime?p=985573#post985573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something to consider as we drift away from the initial complaint, is that the newer production models allows Onyx Path to take a middle ground approach to these sorts of things:<br /> <br /> They can sell Legacies individually/in small groups as cheap pdfs, and sell a big book of them. The big book will be cheaper than each individually, but if you only find 1/3 of them worth using, you can just get those.<br /> <br /> While I like mechanics (including Legacies) presented in supplements to highlight their themes, I also appreciate having the big books of z-splats because there's a lot of cool ideas that might not get published because they're not appropriate to a specific supplement.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I will take more bloodlines and legacies any way that I can get them. Lodges in 2nd Edition have been growing on me as well. I would even be willing to pay for 'DLC content' where one legacy is released at a time and sold for 99 cents or something. That seems the worst case scenario to me, but I'd unquestionably do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11726-solana","name":"Solana","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11726_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T07:25:18-07:00","id":986117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/983778-something-gross-in-legacies-the-sublime?p=985745#post985745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Some of us adored the Legacy books and learned a lot about making our own by following the themes over a course of a book.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ManusDomine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/983778-something-gross-in-legacies-the-sublime?p=985408#post985408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I find the Bloodline books infinitely better and more useful than the Legacy books.<br /> <br /> And then I see the Legacy books as <i>waaaaaaay</i> better than the Lodge books.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Legacy books are acceptable, but I would like books with other things than simply more Legacies in them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T14:34:35-07:00","id":988405,"title":"","content":"I'm hoping for more Legacy books, and more Bloodline books, and more Night Horrors books. I don't know if it's an autism thing or not, but I just really love lists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T15:01:12-07:00","id":988428,"title":"","content":"I would welcome a few legacy books, but far more if the theme of the book was an interesting topic with rules everyone could tap and the legacies were interacting with.<br /> <br /> IMnsHO, <i>Left Hand Path</i> spent <b>too</b> much time on fluff (most of it was obvious, so was tedious to read) but the descriptions of how the factions worked were welcome.<br /> <br /> A compromise between that sort of supplement and the old legacy encyclopedia would be welcome. <br /> <br /> <br /> A few things I'd like to see:<br /> <br /> A book on magical crafts with a list of related legacies.<br /> A full-fledged source book on Awakened Alchemy, all intricate and optional; It could comfortably include 2e Uncrowned Kings (fleshed out and expanded like Tremere in LHP, say) and a few others.<br /> Abyssal practices, so not (just) a list of scelesti legacies, and not <i>Intruders: The Reprint</i>, but focus on other aspects of the Abyss and its power in the world. The Abyssal Shard and Disbelief (Cover a minor template for the people who go towards the Abyss rather than away from it when exposed to Supernal magic), Abyssal intelligences and their effects such as tainted spirits and truly abyssal entities, Abyssal Awakened and, Quippothic Arcana, and so forth. Could include Banisher legacies here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T15:59:28-07:00","id":988480,"title":"","content":"My only problem with the fluff in Left Hand Path is where it covered fluff detailed in other books. Otherwise, great book, wish I saw it earlier for the Scelesti expansion alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T16:53:03-07:00","id":988519,"title":"","content":"Well, that's what I meant. LHP extrapolated in obvious ways from stuff already published---Wasn't suggesting &quot;all of Awakening&quot; was obvious.<br /> <br /> Some fun new elements like the Mad &amp; the sections on dangerous practices like multiple legacies/extra attainments were interesting but <b>under</b>developed. That's why it was frustrating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}